        "original_id": "df221efa-4a55-5209-8e78-e9e89939b284",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gordonia, Osbeckia\n- Plant families: Theaceae, Melastomataceae\n- Related genera: Franklinia, Camellia, Stewartia\n- Place: Gordonia-Alatamaha State Park, Altamaha River\n\nFacts:\n- Gordonia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Theaceae.\n- Gordonia is related to the genera Franklinia, Camellia, and Stewartia.\n- Osbeckia is a genus of plants in the family Melastomataceae.\n- Gordonia-Alatamaha State Park is named for the nearby Altamaha River and the park's nearly extinct Gordonia tree.",
